<p class="lp-small">The current names are Core, Advanced and Max, replacing Enterprise, Unlimited and Agentforce 1. Starter is available monthly or annually; the other listed rates require annual billing.</p>
<h3 class="dg-subheading">What 1, 3 or 5 users cost in year one.</h3>
{{ g.table('Annual subscriptions plus HubSpot’s published required onboarding fee; USD',['Selected plan','1 user','3 users','5 users'],guide.costRows) }}
<p class="lp-small">Totals use the annual rates above × paid seats × 12. HubSpot includes $1,500 onboarding. monday’s one-user total buys its minimum three seats. Other setup, migration, usage and optional products are additional.</p>
<div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>Salesforce extras can change the budget.</h3><p>Sales Engagement is listed at $50/user/month, billed annually, when purchased separately. Adding it for five Core users takes the licence subtotal from <strong>$11,700 to $14,700 a year</strong>.</p><p>Premier Success is already included in Core, Advanced and Max. Pay for an add-on only when your edition leaves a real gap.</p>{{ g.sources([['Salesforce add-ons','https://www.salesforce.com/sales/pricing/add-ons/']]) }}</div><div><h3>The cheapest licence can still be expensive to run.</h3><p>Get setup and ongoing administration priced separately. Include data mapping, integrations, reports, permissions and training.</p><p>Salesforce publishes no fixed implementation price. Get a quote for your setup.</p></div></div>
{{ g.midcta(guide,'Need help working the leads already in your CRM?','CallTeam can make the calls, qualify interest and handle follow-up while your team focuses on sales conversations.') }}
