<section class="lp-section" id="switching"><div class="lp-wrap">
{{ g.heading('05','Price the move','How to leave Salesforce<br>without losing the useful work.','A cheaper subscription is only part of the switching decision.') }}
<ol class="dg-steps"><li><strong>Save the connected records.</strong> Export accounts, contacts, leads, deals, notes and activities. Keep the IDs that link them, and check attachment access.</li><li><strong>Keep the workflows people use.</strong> List the reports, routing rules and permissions that matter. Leave unused customisations out of the rebuild.</li><li><strong>Test a small sample.</strong> Import representative records. Make a call, log the result, schedule a follow-up and hand a deal to another rep.</li><li><strong>Price the transition.</strong> Add migration, training, integrations and any period when both systems stay active.</li><li><strong>Agree on the cutover.</strong> Check the imported records and responsibilities before cancelling access to the old system.</li></ol>
<p class="dg-related">If you are changing the sales process too, use our <a href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">free campaign planner</a> to agree on targeting, qualification and the next step.</p>
</div></section>
